<title>INDIA: India forex reserves rise to $26.56 bln on Apr 17.</title>
<headline>India forex reserves rise to $26.56 bln on Apr 17.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-04-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's foreign exchange reserves rose to $26.56 billon on April 17, up from $26.49 billion a week ago, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said in its weekly statistical supplement on Saturday.</p>
<p>	 Foreign exchange reserves (in million U.S. dollars)</p>
<p>					  Apr 11	Apr 11	 Apr 19</p>
<p>					   1997	  1997	   1996</p>
<p>    Foreign currency assets     22,509	22,435	 17,208</p>
<p>    Gold				 4,054	 4,054	  4,561</p>
<p>    SDRs				     2	     2	     42</p>
<p>    Total			     26,565	26,491	 21,811</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
